WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.609
- Good morning, BelieveNation.

00:00:01.609 --> 00:00:02.879
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.879 --> 00:00:04.381
My one word is believe

00:00:04.381 --> 00:00:06.431
and I believe that entrepreneurs are going

00:00:06.431 --> 00:00:09.420
to solve all of the
world's major problems.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.904
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:10.904 --> 00:00:13.410
today's message is break the rules.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.559
Over to you, Georges St. Pierre.

00:00:15.559 --> 00:00:17.484
(rooster crowing)

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:20.058
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:20.058 --> 00:00:22.981
♫ Entspresso keep me going.

00:00:22.981 --> 00:00:26.984
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:26.984 --> 00:00:30.377
- I've never been afraid
to break the rules in life.

00:00:30.377 --> 00:00:32.426
I'm not talking about break the law.

00:00:32.426 --> 00:00:34.070
Break the rules.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:36.832
Why would you want to be in this world

00:00:36.832 --> 00:00:39.665
if it's to be like everybody else?

00:00:40.853 --> 00:00:43.279
The most successful people
in life are the ones

00:00:43.279 --> 00:00:45.030
that are doing the things out,

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:47.424
they are thinking outside of the box.

00:00:47.424 --> 00:00:50.246
So don't be afraid to break the rules.

00:00:50.246 --> 00:00:52.163
- So I've never been a huge fan of rules

00:00:52.163 --> 00:00:53.431
and I'm guessing if you're an entrepreneur

00:00:53.431 --> 00:00:54.490
and you're watching this channel,

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:56.188
you're not a big fan of rules either.

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:58.649
Entrepreneurs in general,
we are rule breakers.

00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:00.541
We like to create new things,

00:01:00.541 --> 00:01:01.966
we like to push the boundaries,

00:01:01.966 --> 00:01:05.156
we want to change the way
things are done in our industry

00:01:05.156 --> 00:01:06.297
(gentle music)

00:01:06.297 --> 00:01:07.174
and so for that to happen,

00:01:07.174 --> 00:01:09.370
we have to break some of the rules.

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:11.486
I think the rules are important

00:01:11.486 --> 00:01:14.308
and just to understand that rules are here

00:01:14.308 --> 00:01:17.975
to keep average people
doing average things.

00:01:18.854 --> 00:01:20.805
And there's a lot of things in life

00:01:20.805 --> 00:01:22.516
that you are average at.

00:01:22.516 --> 00:01:24.312
Most things, you are average

00:01:24.312 --> 00:01:27.479
or maybe even below average in life at

00:01:28.399 --> 00:01:30.391
and so the rules can help you.

00:01:30.391 --> 00:01:32.394
The rules can help you stay safe.

00:01:32.394 --> 00:01:34.435
The rules can help you get by.

00:01:34.435 --> 00:01:37.998
You know, if you're in the
emergency exit of an airplane,

00:01:37.998 --> 00:01:40.787
they have rules that you're
supposed to abide by.

00:01:40.787 --> 00:01:43.070
Unless you're an airline security expert,

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:44.941
like, follow the rules.

00:01:44.941 --> 00:01:48.020
The mask comes down, put
it on your face, right?

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:49.393
There are rules to follow

00:01:49.393 --> 00:01:51.192
that if you don't know anything better,

00:01:51.192 --> 00:01:52.279
just follow the rules.

00:01:52.279 --> 00:01:54.486
It'll help keep you on the average.

00:01:54.486 --> 00:01:57.798
But for the things that
you're way above average on,

00:01:57.798 --> 00:02:00.400
for the things that you
have genius level talent at

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.399
and you could be one of
the best in the world at,

00:02:02.399 --> 00:02:03.801
for those things,

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:06.034
then you have to adopt the mentality

00:02:06.034 --> 00:02:08.112
of I'm going to break the rules.

00:02:08.112 --> 00:02:10.007
There's this great clip of Steve Jobs

00:02:10.007 --> 00:02:12.084
who was doing an interview

00:02:12.084 --> 00:02:14.570
and he was talking about
how the world is made up

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:17.034
by people who are no smarter than you.

00:02:17.034 --> 00:02:18.359
The rules that are in place

00:02:18.359 --> 00:02:20.484
were put there by another human being

00:02:20.484 --> 00:02:22.446
who is no smarter than you

00:02:22.446 --> 00:02:24.565
and if you are an expert in your industry,

00:02:24.565 --> 00:02:26.432
you're probably smarter than them.

00:02:26.432 --> 00:02:29.413
And so don't live your
life and run your business

00:02:29.413 --> 00:02:33.757
according to rules that are
old and created by people

00:02:33.757 --> 00:02:36.692
who aren't as much of
an expert as you are.

00:02:36.692 --> 00:02:38.554
I think a lot of people
are afraid to break a rule

00:02:38.554 --> 00:02:40.749
because that's the way
that it's always done.

00:02:40.749 --> 00:02:41.902
And I'm not suggesting go out

00:02:41.902 --> 00:02:43.387
and do something that's illegal,

00:02:43.387 --> 00:02:45.692
'cause that's a whole other can of worms,

00:02:45.692 --> 00:02:48.651
but the way things are
traditionally done in an industry.

00:02:48.651 --> 00:02:51.446
A lot of times it doesn't
even make sense anymore.

00:02:51.446 --> 00:02:54.754
And that's on you to not
just break the rules,

00:02:54.754 --> 00:02:57.610
but to create the new standard.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.419
So I'd look at my YouTube channel.

00:02:59.419 --> 00:03:01.204
I just came back from
ClamourCon as an example

00:03:01.204 --> 00:03:03.524
which is an event for YouTubers

00:03:03.524 --> 00:03:06.693
and a lot of these guys are
publishing one video a week

00:03:06.693 --> 00:03:09.071
or a video every two weeks

00:03:09.071 --> 00:03:11.435
and part of the YouTube algorithm

00:03:11.435 --> 00:03:13.785
that's really important
is consistent content.

00:03:13.785 --> 00:03:16.575
Once a day is really
going to be the minimum.

00:03:16.575 --> 00:03:17.941
When I went from once a week

00:03:17.941 --> 00:03:19.518
to once a day, my channel shot up.

00:03:19.518 --> 00:03:21.555
When I went from once
a day to twice a day,

00:03:21.555 --> 00:03:22.926
my channel shot up again.

00:03:22.926 --> 00:03:24.660
From twice a day to three times a day,

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:27.092
not as much, doesn't really
make a huge difference.

00:03:27.092 --> 00:03:28.792
It still goes up but you don't get

00:03:28.792 --> 00:03:31.076
the same returns as the other ones.

00:03:31.076 --> 00:03:34.193
And so everybody's saying wow,
I don't know how you do it,

00:03:34.193 --> 00:03:36.274
I don't know how you build up that team

00:03:36.274 --> 00:03:39.289
and we're responding
to every single comment

00:03:39.289 --> 00:03:41.744
and we're updating our tags
and descriptions and titles

00:03:41.744 --> 00:03:43.637
and testing thumbnails
and doing all these things

00:03:43.637 --> 00:03:45.700
that most people aren't doing on YouTube

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.858
and that's why I've had the success

00:03:47.858 --> 00:03:50.078
that other people haven't.

00:03:50.078 --> 00:03:52.752
And so it's setting a new standard.

00:03:52.752 --> 00:03:54.567
Right, breaking the rules that people

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.597
thought were important
before and saying no,

00:03:56.597 --> 00:03:59.280
this is the new path to
go and come and follow me

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.266
and I think if you have that ability,

00:04:01.266 --> 00:04:03.583
you have that genius
level talent at something,

00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:05.287
you are the expert in your industry.

00:04:05.287 --> 00:04:09.387
It's not only what you
should be doing for yourself.

00:04:09.387 --> 00:04:13.432
It's your obligation to go
out and create a new standard

00:04:13.432 --> 00:04:17.273
for your industry and not
play to a smaller level

00:04:17.273 --> 00:04:20.084
just because there are
some rules in place.

00:04:20.084 --> 00:04:21.642
So the question of the
day today is, I'm curious,

00:04:21.642 --> 00:04:23.178
what is the single biggest rule

00:04:23.178 --> 00:04:24.831
that you want to break in your industry?

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:26.483
What is the rule that drives you nuts

00:04:26.483 --> 00:04:28.743
that you want to abolish and say,

00:04:28.743 --> 00:04:30.423
this is the new way.

00:04:30.423 --> 00:04:32.672
I'm curious, leave it down
in the comments below.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.377
I also want to give a quick shout out

00:04:34.377 --> 00:04:36.448
to Diana Gartland from dianagartland.com.

00:04:36.448 --> 00:04:38.926
Thank you so much for picking up a copy

00:04:38.926 --> 00:04:40.137
of my book, Your One Word, Diana.

00:04:40.137 --> 00:04:41.233
I really, really, really appreciate it

00:04:41.233 --> 00:04:43.323
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:04:43.323 --> 00:04:45.162
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:04:45.162 --> 00:04:46.202
I believe in you.

00:04:46.202 --> 00:04:48.010
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:50.077
and whatever your one word is.

00:04:50.077 --> 00:04:52.597
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:04:52.597 --> 00:04:55.432
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:04:55.432 --> 00:04:57.651
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:04:57.651 --> 00:05:01.318
♫ Entspresso keep me going.

00:05:04.626 --> 00:05:06.777
- We have so many rules
in life about everything.

00:05:06.777 --> 00:05:10.099
I say break the rules, not
the law, but break the rules.

00:05:10.099 --> 00:05:13.203
My wife has a T-shirt that says

00:05:13.203 --> 00:05:17.158
well behaved women rarely make history.

00:05:17.158 --> 00:05:19.964
Well you know, I don't
want to burst her bubble,

00:05:19.964 --> 00:05:22.001
but the same is true with men.

00:05:22.001 --> 00:05:24.762
It is impossible to be a
maverick or true original

00:05:24.762 --> 00:05:26.484
if you're too well behaved

00:05:26.484 --> 00:05:28.714
and don't want to break the rules.

00:05:28.714 --> 00:05:30.877
You have to think outside the box,

00:05:30.877 --> 00:05:32.685
that's what I believe after all.

00:05:32.685 --> 00:05:34.470
What is the point of being on this earth

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:35.960
if all you want to do is be liked

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:38.278
by everyone and avoid trouble?

00:05:38.278 --> 00:05:40.990
The only way that I ever got any place

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:43.892
was by breaking some of the rules.

00:05:43.892 --> 00:05:46.020
After all, I remember
that after I was finished

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.600
with my body building career,
I wanted to get into acting

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:51.519
and I wanted to be a star in films.

00:05:51.519 --> 00:05:53.739
You can imagine what the agent said

00:05:53.739 --> 00:05:55.936
when I went to meet all those agents.

00:05:55.936 --> 00:05:58.397
Everyone had the same line
that it can't be done.

00:05:58.397 --> 00:06:00.584
The rules are different here.

00:06:00.584 --> 00:06:03.583
Just look at your body, you
have this huge, monstrous body,

00:06:03.583 --> 00:06:07.266
overly developed, that
doesn't fit into the movies.

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:08.474
You don't understand.

00:06:08.474 --> 00:06:11.353
This was 20 years ago the Hercules movies.

00:06:11.353 --> 00:06:13.668
Now there is the little guys that are in,

00:06:13.668 --> 00:06:16.962
Dustin Hoffman, Woody
Allen, Jack Nicholson,

00:06:16.962 --> 00:06:20.112
before he gained weight of course that is.

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:22.554
But anyway those are the guys that win.

00:06:22.554 --> 00:06:24.626
And the agent also
complained about my accent.

00:06:24.626 --> 00:06:27.338
He said no one ever became a
star with an accent like that.

00:06:27.338 --> 00:06:29.084
Especially not with a German accent

00:06:29.084 --> 00:06:31.201
and yes, I can imagine with your name,

00:06:31.201 --> 00:06:34.192
Arnold Schwarzen, Schnitzel
or whatever the name is,

00:06:34.192 --> 00:06:36.747
on a billboard, yeah that's
going to draw a lot of tickets

00:06:36.747 --> 00:06:39.112
and sell a lot of tickets, yeah right.

00:06:39.112 --> 00:06:41.374
So this is the kind of
negative attitude they had,

00:06:41.374 --> 00:06:43.873
but I didn't listen to those rules,

00:06:43.873 --> 00:06:45.776
even though they were very
nice and they said look,

00:06:45.776 --> 00:06:47.431
we can get you some good parts.

00:06:47.431 --> 00:06:51.349
We can get you to be playing
a wrestler or bouncer

00:06:51.349 --> 00:06:53.896
or maybe with your German
accent we can get you

00:06:53.896 --> 00:06:56.674
to be a Nazi officer in Hogan's Heroes

00:06:56.674 --> 00:06:58.420
or something like that.

00:06:58.420 --> 00:07:00.602
But I didn't listen to all this.

00:07:00.602 --> 00:07:03.126
These were there rules, not my rules.

00:07:03.126 --> 00:07:05.115
I was convinced I could do it.

00:07:05.115 --> 00:07:07.292
That if I worked as hard
as I did in body building,

00:07:07.292 --> 00:07:10.169
five hours a day, and I
started getting the work,

00:07:10.169 --> 00:07:13.352
I started taking acting
classes, took English classes,

00:07:13.352 --> 00:07:16.116
took speech classes, dialogue classes,

00:07:16.116 --> 00:07:19.041
accent removal classes I even took.

00:07:19.041 --> 00:07:23.489
I remember running around a
fine wine rose and a vine,

00:07:23.489 --> 00:07:25.469
you see because Germans have difficulties

00:07:25.469 --> 00:07:27.327
with the F and the W and the V

00:07:27.327 --> 00:07:29.838
so fine wise rose and a vine.

00:07:29.838 --> 00:07:31.537
I know what some of you now say

00:07:31.537 --> 00:07:33.713
is I hope that Arnold got his money back,

00:07:33.713 --> 00:07:35.659
but let me tell you something,

00:07:35.659 --> 00:07:37.292
I had a good times doing those things

00:07:37.292 --> 00:07:38.527
and it really helped me.

00:07:38.527 --> 00:07:40.152
And finally I broke through.

00:07:40.152 --> 00:07:42.665
I broke through and I started
getting the first parts

00:07:42.665 --> 00:07:46.491
in TV, Streets of San Francisco,
Lucille Ball hired me.

00:07:46.491 --> 00:07:48.709
I made Pumping Iron, Stay Hungry,

00:07:48.709 --> 00:07:51.656
and then I got the big break
in Conan the Barbarian.

00:07:51.656 --> 00:07:53.872
(audience cheering)

00:07:53.872 --> 00:07:55.555
And there the director said

00:07:55.555 --> 00:07:56.987
if we wouldn't have Schwarzenegger,

00:07:56.987 --> 00:07:58.969
we would have to build one.

00:07:58.969 --> 00:08:00.316
Now think about that.

00:08:00.316 --> 00:08:03.369
And then when I did
Terminator, I'll be back

00:08:03.369 --> 00:08:05.444
(audience cheering)

00:08:05.444 --> 00:08:09.719
became one of the most
famous lines in movie history

00:08:09.719 --> 00:08:13.069
all because of my crazy accent.

00:08:13.069 --> 00:08:14.258
Now think about it.

00:08:14.258 --> 00:08:15.927
The things that the agents said

00:08:15.927 --> 00:08:18.437
would be totally a detriment,

00:08:18.437 --> 00:08:20.386
it would be impossible
for me to get a job,

00:08:20.386 --> 00:08:22.702
all of a sudden became an asset for me.

00:08:22.702 --> 00:08:25.134
All of those things, my
accent, my body and everything,

00:08:25.134 --> 00:08:26.868
so it just shows to you never listen

00:08:26.868 --> 00:08:29.035
that you can't do something.

00:08:29.035 --> 00:08:31.328
And you have to work
your way up, of course.

00:08:31.328 --> 00:08:32.908
Run for something else first.

00:08:32.908 --> 00:08:34.285
I mean it was the same

00:08:34.285 --> 00:08:36.905
when I ran for governor.

00:08:36.905 --> 00:08:39.191
The same lines that if they work you up,

00:08:39.191 --> 00:08:41.328
it can't be done, and then of course,

00:08:41.328 --> 00:08:43.648
I ran for governor and the
rest of course is history.

00:08:43.648 --> 00:08:45.954
They said you have to start
with a small jump as mayor

00:08:45.954 --> 00:08:48.820
and then as assemblyman and
then as lieutenant governor

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:51.198
and then as governor and they said that's

00:08:51.198 --> 00:08:53.413
the way it works in the political career.

00:08:53.413 --> 00:08:55.671
I said I'm not interested
in a political career.

00:08:55.671 --> 00:08:57.467
I want to be a public servant.

00:08:57.467 --> 00:08:59.359
I want to fix California's problems

00:08:59.359 --> 00:09:02.049
and bring people together and
bring the parties together.

00:09:02.049 --> 00:09:03.815
So like I said, I decided to run.

00:09:03.815 --> 00:09:05.666
I didn't pay attention to the rules

00:09:05.666 --> 00:09:09.243
and I made it and the rest is history.

00:09:09.243 --> 00:09:10.821
- Let me tell you a story.

00:09:10.821 --> 00:09:12.706
So a friend of mine and I,

00:09:12.706 --> 00:09:14.800
we went for a run in Central Park.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:16.934
The Road Runners organization,

00:09:16.934 --> 00:09:19.444
on the weekends, they host races.

00:09:19.444 --> 00:09:21.464
And it's very common
at the end of the race

00:09:21.464 --> 00:09:23.871
they'll have a sponsor who
will give away something,

00:09:23.871 --> 00:09:25.999
apples or bagels or something.

00:09:25.999 --> 00:09:27.533
And on this particular day,

00:09:27.533 --> 00:09:29.205
when we got to the end of the run,

00:09:29.205 --> 00:09:31.014
there were some free bagels

00:09:31.014 --> 00:09:33.773
and they had picnic tables set up

00:09:33.773 --> 00:09:36.855
and on one side was a group of volunteers.

00:09:36.855 --> 00:09:38.880
On the table were boxes of bagels.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:42.160
And on the other side it
was a long line of runners

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:44.586
waiting to get their free bagel.

00:09:44.586 --> 00:09:47.134
So I said to my friend, let's get a bagel.

00:09:47.134 --> 00:09:48.994
And he looked at me and said,

00:09:48.994 --> 00:09:51.156
that line's too long.

00:09:51.156 --> 00:09:53.073
And I said, free bagel.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:58.142
And he said, I don't want to wait in line.

00:09:58.142 --> 00:10:01.028
And I was like, free bagel.

00:10:01.028 --> 00:10:03.067
(audience laughter)

00:10:03.067 --> 00:10:05.232
And he says nah, it's too long.

00:10:05.232 --> 00:10:06.794
And that's when I realized

00:10:06.794 --> 00:10:09.172
that there's two ways to see the world.

00:10:09.172 --> 00:10:11.943
Some people see the thing that they want

00:10:11.943 --> 00:10:14.415
and some people see the
thing that prevents them

00:10:14.415 --> 00:10:16.753
from getting the thing that they want.

00:10:16.753 --> 00:10:18.735
I could only see the bagels.

00:10:18.735 --> 00:10:21.549
He could only see the line.

00:10:21.549 --> 00:10:24.132
And so I walked up to the line.

00:10:25.608 --> 00:10:28.191
I leaned in between two people,

00:10:29.837 --> 00:10:33.384
put my hand in the box,
and pulled out two bagels.

00:10:33.384 --> 00:10:35.200
And no one got mad at me

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:38.407
because the rule is you can
go after whatever you want,

00:10:38.407 --> 00:10:40.668
you just cannot deny anyone else

00:10:40.668 --> 00:10:43.187
to go after whatever they want.

00:10:43.187 --> 00:10:45.226
Now I had to sacrifice choice.

00:10:45.226 --> 00:10:47.098
I didn't get to choose which bagel I got.

00:10:47.098 --> 00:10:48.787
I got whatever I pulled out.

00:10:48.787 --> 00:10:51.102
But I didn't have to wait in line.

00:10:51.102 --> 00:10:53.501
So the point is is you
don't have to wait in line.

00:10:53.501 --> 00:10:56.100
You don't have to do it the
way everybody else has done it.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:57.701
You can do it your way.

00:10:57.701 --> 00:10:59.248
You can break the rules.

00:10:59.248 --> 00:11:00.825
You just can't get in the way

00:11:00.825 --> 00:11:02.764
of somebody else getting what they want.

00:11:02.764 --> 00:11:04.412
That's rule number one.

